=== Technical Question ===
Question: I get this error in my php code: "Call to undefined method App\Controller\UserController::getName()" - this is my line of code: $user->getName() where $user is an instance of User entity.

Answer: That message means PHP thinks $user is an instance of App\Controller\UserController (your controller class), not your entity. Common causes and how to fix:

1) Verify what $user actually is
- Dump its class: var_dump(get_class($user)); die; (or dump($user) / dd($user) in Symfony).
